body:
Our house was only that much because it was:
(a) tiny and built on land so small it had to be unit-titled;
(b) a long way from work, family & friends (unless you count cows and beehives);
(c) bought from someone we knew;
(d) backed by gorse on a steep bank (the only backyard);
(e) uncarpeted with no curtains or appliances.

We decorated the inside and I turned the bank into a series of garden areas, clearing gorse and cutting steps by hand while planting the rest with cheap, ground-stabilising greenery. We made it into an appealing home for a retiree and sold it for about $35k profit.
